## Commands

Run Maven from the project root. `./mvnw` is the Maven wrapper; when the project has none, use `mvn` (`./dev.sh` falls back on its own).

### Build and test

```bash
./mvnw package                    # compile, unit tests, the JAR<!-- IF frontend=embedded --> with the SPA built into it<!-- END frontend -->
<!-- IF frontend=embedded -->
./mvnw package -Pskip-frontend    # the same without Node/npm, for backend-only work
./mvnw verify -Pskip-frontend     # + integration tests (Docker) + regenerates contracts/openapi.json
<!-- END frontend -->
<!-- IF frontend!=embedded -->
./mvnw verify                     # + integration tests (Docker) + regenerates contracts/openapi.json
<!-- END frontend -->
./mvnw -pl backend test -Dtest=ClassName             # one unit test class
./mvnw -pl backend test -Dtest="ClassName#method"    # one unit test method
```

Integration tests (`*IT`, `*IntegrationTest`) run under Failsafe on `verify` and need Docker: each test JVM starts one {{db_label}} container through `IntegrationTestBase`.

### Inner-loop integration tests (RED → GREEN iteration)

While iterating to make a failing test go green, run **only the changed IT class**, compiling first so the test does not run stale bytecode:

```bash
./mvnw -pl backend test-compile failsafe:integration-test failsafe:verify -Dit.test=ChangedIT
./mvnw -pl backend test-compile failsafe:integration-test failsafe:verify -Dit.test='ChangedIT#method_name'
```

Run full `./mvnw verify` once at the end of GREEN, before the save-point commit.

`IntegrationTestBase` already follows the fast-suite recipe: one container per JVM<!-- IF db!=mongo -->, data in RAM<!-- END db -->, and a small Spring context cache that makes a second context visible. What keeps that recipe safe with Essentials — truncate read-model tables only, **never an `*_events` table with `RESTART IDENTITY`**, and rebuild a read model through `onSubscriptionsReset` plus `resetAllSubscriptions()` — is in the `essentials-docs` skill (`LLM-foundation-test.md` § Fast integration tests). Container reuse across builds is opt-in there.

